In a short callback exercise, a interviewer presents the trace below. The team wants to know what this code logs:
let total = 0;
for (const x of [1600, 2, 3]) { total += x; }
console.log(total);
In this run, what total is printed?

Consider the following JavaScript statements:
const obj = { a: 1601, b: 2 };
let keys = '';
for (const p in obj) { keys += p; }
console.log(keys.length);
What length is logged?

In a short callback exercise, a interviewer shares this program. A student submits the snippet below for review:
console.log('start');
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log(1602));
